<title>UK: Country Casuals cuts H1 loss, lifts div.</title>
<headline>Country Casuals cuts H1 loss, lifts div.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-10-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>half year to July 27</p>
<p>			   (million stg unless stated)</p>
<p> Shr (pence)		3.07 loss	    vs 3.47 loss</p>
<p> Dividend (pence)	 1.70		   vs 1.41</p>
<p> Pretax		     0.9 loss	     vs 1.0  loss</p>
<p> Turnover		   23.7		   vs 22.8</p>
<p> Operating result	 0.8 loss	     vs 1.1 loss</p>
<p> Exceptional		nil		    vs nil</p>
<p> Interest (payable)     0.1		    vs nil</p>
<p> Tax			  0.3		    vs 0.4</p>
<p> Net taxed		  0.6 loss	     vs 0.7 loss</p>
<p> Retained		   0.9 loss	     vs 0.9 loss</p>
<p> Pay date		   December 16</p>
<p> Div registration date  October 29</p>
<p>NOTE - Clothes retailer Country Casual Holdings Plc said the second half of the year began well in August but was below expectations in September, with overall sales two percent ahead of the same period a year earlier.  </p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
